    " np:[\"Denali\",\"Gates of the Arctic\",\"Glacier Bay\",\"Katmai\",\"Kenai Fjords\",\"Kobuk Valley\",\"Lake Clark\",\"Wrangell-St. Elias\"],\n",
    " geo:\"Larger than Texas, California and Montana combined. The Brooks Range divides the Arctic North Slope from the interior; the Alaska Range carries the continent's highest summit; the Aleutian arc runs 1,200 miles into the Pacific. Roughly half of U.S. glacier ice lies here.\",\n",
    " feat:[\"Denali\",\"Wrangell-St. Elias (largest U.S. national park)\",\"Aleutian volcanic arc\",\"Prince William Sound\",\"North Slope tundra\",\"Inside Passage\"],\n",
    " riv:[\"Yukon\",\"Kuskokwim\",\"Tanana\",\"Copper\"],rng:[\"Brooks Range\",\"Alaska Range\",\"Chugach\",\"Wrangell\",\"Aleutian Range\"],\n",
    " cty:[\"Anchorage\",\"Fairbanks\",\"Juneau\",\"Wasilla\",\"Sitka\"],\n",
    " econ:\"North Slope petroleum, commercial fisheries (the largest U.S. catch by volume), mining, federal and military installations, and tourism.\",\n",
    " hist:\"Purchased from Russia in 1867 for $7.2 million. Gold rushes from 1898; the Trans-Alaska Pipeline opened 1977. Statehood came in 1959, the 49th state.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "AZ:{n:\"Arizona\",cap:\"Phoenix\",big:\"Phoenix\",adm:\"February 14, 1912\",ord:48,pop:7623818,pr:14,area:113990,ar:6,nick:\"Grand Canyon State\",reg:\"West\",div:\"Mountain\",tz:\"Mountain (no daylight saving, except Navajo Nation)\",\n",
    " hi:[\"Humphreys Peak\",12633],lo:[\"Colorado River at Yuma\",70],np:[\"Grand Canyon\",\"Petrified Forest\",\"Saguaro\"],\n",
    " geo:\"Three provinces: the Colorado Plateau in the north, cut by the Grand Canyon; the Mogollon Rim escarpment; and the Basin and Range desert of the south. The Sonoran Desert here is the only place the saguaro cactus grows wild.\",\n",
    " feat:[\"Grand Canyon\",\"Monument Valley\",\"Painted Desert\",\"Sonoran Desert\",\"Meteor Crater\",\"Havasu Falls\"],\n",
    " riv:[\"Colorado\",\"Gila\",\"Salt\",\"Little Colorado\"],rng:[\"Mogollon Rim\",\"San Francisco Peaks\",\"Chiricahua Mountains\"],\n",
    " cty:[\"Phoenix\",\"Tucson\",\"Mesa\",\"Chandler\",\"Gilbert\"],\n",
    " econ:\"Semiconductors and electronics, aerospace, copper mining (the leading U.S. producer), tourism, and retirement migration.\",\n",
    " hist:\"Acquired from Mexico in 1848 and by the Gadsden Purchase of 1853. Long a territory owing to disputes over slavery and Mormon settlement, it entered the Union last of the contiguous states in 1912.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "AR:{n:\"Arkansas\",cap:\"Little Rock\",big:\"Little Rock\",adm:\"June 15, 1836\",ord:25,pop:3114791,pr:33,area:53179,ar:29,nick:\"The Natural State\",reg:\"South\",div:\"West South Central\",tz:\"Central\",\n",
