    " geo:\"Glacial till plains in the north and center; the unglaciated south is hillier, with karst caves and the Ohio River bluffs. Forty-five miles of Lake Michigan shoreline hold the Indiana Dunes.\",\n",
    " feat:[\"Indiana Dunes\",\"Wyandotte Caves\",\"Brown County hills\",\"Ohio River valley\"],\n",
    " riv:[\"Ohio\",\"Wabash\",\"White\",\"Tippecanoe\"],rng:[\"Knobstone Escarpment\"],\n",
    " cty:[\"Indianapolis\",\"Fort Wayne\",\"Evansville\",\"Carmel\",\"South Bend\"],\n",
    " econ:\"The most manufacturing-intensive state by share of output: steel at Gary, vehicles, pharmaceuticals at Indianapolis, and orthopedic devices at Warsaw.\",\n",
    " hist:\"Admitted 1816. The Battle of Tippecanoe in 1811 broke Tecumseh's confederacy. The Indianapolis 500 has run since 1911.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "IA:{n:\"Iowa\",cap:\"Des Moines\",big:\"Des Moines\",adm:\"December 28, 1846\",ord:29,pop:3238387,pr:32,area:56273,ar:26,nick:\"Hawkeye State\",reg:\"Midwest\",div:\"West North Central\",tz:\"Central\",\n",
