    " hist:\"The Toledo War of 1835-36 with Ohio ended with Michigan surrendering Toledo and receiving the Upper Peninsula. The moving assembly line began at Highland Park in 1913.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "MN:{n:\"Minnesota\",cap:\"St. Paul\",big:\"Minneapolis\",adm:\"May 11, 1858\",ord:32,pop:5830405,pr:22,area:86936,ar:12,nick:\"North Star State\",reg:\"Midwest\",div:\"West North Central\",tz:\"Central\",\n",
    " hi:[\"Eagle Mountain\",2301],lo:[\"Lake Superior\",601],np:[\"Voyageurs\"],\n",
    " geo:\"Water flows from here to three destinations: the Gulf of Mexico via the Mississippi, Hudson Bay via the Red River, and the Atlantic via the Great Lakes. Roughly 11,800 lakes over ten acres. The Northwest Angle is the only part of the lower 48 north of the 49th parallel.\",\n",
