    " hist:\"Admitted 1817. The Delta produced the blues, and Highway 61 carried it north. Site of much of the hardest fighting of the civil rights era, including the Freedom Summer of 1964.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "MO:{n:\"Missouri\",cap:\"Jefferson City\",big:\"Kansas City\",adm:\"August 10, 1821\",ord:24,pop:6270541,pr:18,area:69707,ar:21,nick:\"Show-Me State\",reg:\"Midwest\",div:\"West North Central\",tz:\"Central\",\n",
    " hi:[\"Taum Sauk Mountain\",1772],lo:[\"St. Francis River\",230],np:[\"Gateway Arch\"],\n",
    " geo:\"The Missouri and Mississippi meet just above St. Louis. The Ozark Plateau covers the south with some of the world's densest concentrations of springs and caves, over 7,300 recorded. The Bootheel in the southeast is alluvial Delta country.\",\n",
