    "Object.assign(ST, {\n",
    "NE:{n:\"Nebraska\",cap:\"Lincoln\",big:\"Omaha\",adm:\"March 1, 1867\",ord:37,pop:2018006,pr:38,area:77348,ar:16,nick:\"Cornhusker State\",reg:\"Midwest\",div:\"West North Central\",tz:\"Central / Mountain (western panhandle)\",\n",
    " hi:[\"Panorama Point\",5424],lo:[\"Missouri River\",840],np:[],\n",
    " geo:\"The Sandhills cover nearly a quarter of the state, the largest sand dune formation in the Western Hemisphere, held in place by a thin skin of prairie grass. Beneath lies the Ogallala Aquifer, which irrigates much of the High Plains. The land rises steadily westward from 840 to 5,424 feet.\",\n",
    " feat:[\"Sandhills\",\"Chimney Rock\",\"Scotts Bluff\",\"Niobrara River\",\"Toadstool Geologic Park\",\"Ogallala Aquifer\"],\n",
