    " cty:[\"Omaha\",\"Lincoln\",\"Bellevue\",\"Grand Island\",\"Kearney\"],\n",
    " econ:\"Beef and corn, insurance and finance at Omaha (Berkshire Hathaway, Mutual of Omaha), Union Pacific headquarters, and ethanol.\",\n",
    " hist:\"The Kansas-Nebraska Act of 1854 reopened the slavery question and helped precipitate the Civil War. Admitted 1867. Since 1937 it has had the only unicameral and officially nonpartisan legislature in the country.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "NV:{n:\"Nevada\",cap:\"Carson City\",big:\"Las Vegas\",adm:\"October 31, 1864\",ord:36,pop:3282188,pr:31,area:110572,ar:7,nick:\"Silver State\",reg:\"West\",div:\"Mountain\",tz:\"Pacific / Mountain (West Wendover)\",\n",
    " hi:[\"Boundary Peak\",13147],lo:[\"Colorado River\",481],np:[\"Great Basin\"],\n",
    " geo:\"The driest state, averaging about nine inches of precipitation. More than 150 separate mountain ranges run north to south across the Basin and Range, each divided by a closed valley with no outlet to the sea. Roughly 80% of the state is federally owned, the highest share in the nation.\",\n",
    " feat:[\"Great Basin\",\"Lake Tahoe\",\"Valley of Fire\",\"Red Rock Canyon\",\"Black Rock Desert\",\"Ruby Mountains\"],\n",
    " riv:[\"Colorado\",\"Humboldt\",\"Truckee\",\"Carson\"],rng:[\"Sierra Nevada\",\"Ruby Mountains\",\"Toiyabe Range\",\"Snake Range\"],\n",
    " cty:[\"Las Vegas\",\"Henderson\",\"North Las Vegas\",\"Reno\",\"Sparks\"],\n",
    " econ:\"Gaming and tourism, gold mining (the leading U.S. producer), warehousing and logistics, lithium extraction, and data centers.\",\n",
    " hist:\"Admitted in October 1864, days before the presidential election, to strengthen Lincoln and the Thirteenth Amendment, hence the motto 'Battle Born.' The Comstock Lode of 1859 was the richest silver strike in American history.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "NH:{n:\"New Hampshire\",cap:\"Concord\",big:\"Manchester\",adm:\"June 21, 1788\",ord:9,pop:1415342,pr:41,area:9349,ar:46,nick:\"Granite State\",reg:\"Northeast\",div:\"New England\",tz:\"Eastern\",\n",
    " hi:[\"Mount Washington\",6288],lo:[\"Atlantic Ocean\",0],np:[],\n",
    " geo:\"The White Mountains are the highest in the Northeast. Mount Washington recorded a surface wind of 231 miles per hour in April 1934, which stood as the world record for over sixty years. Only 18 miles of coastline, the shortest of any coastal state.\",\n",
    " feat:[\"White Mountains\",\"Mount Washington\",\"Franconia Notch\",\"Lake Winnipesaukee\",\"Isles of Shoals\",\"Flume Gorge\"],\n",
    " riv:[\"Connecticut\",\"Merrimack\",\"Androscoggin\",\"Saco\"],rng:[\"White Mountains\",\"Presidential Range\"],\n",
    " cty:[\"Manchester\",\"Nashua\",\"Concord\",\"Derry\",\"Dover\"],\n",
    " econ:\"Advanced manufacturing and precision machining, tourism, and Boston-area spillover. No general sales tax and no tax on earned income.\",\n",
    " hist:\"First colony to establish a government independent of Britain, in January 1776. Its ratification on June 21, 1788 was the ninth and therefore the one that put the Constitution into effect. Has held the first presidential primary since 1920.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "NJ:{n:\"New Jersey\",cap:\"Trenton\",big:\"Newark\",adm:\"December 18, 1787\",ord:3,pop:9548215,pr:11,area:8723,ar:47,nick:\"Garden State\",reg:\"Northeast\",div:\"Middle Atlantic\",tz:\"Eastern\",\n",
    " hi:[\"High Point\",1803],lo:[\"Atlantic Ocean\",0],np:[],\n",
    " geo:\"The most densely populated state, at roughly 1,300 people per square mile. Despite that, the Pine Barrens covers over a million acres of pitch pine forest above the Kirkwood-Cohansey aquifer, one of the largest bodies of fresh water on the East Coast.\",\n",
    " feat:[\"Pine Barrens\",\"Delaware Water Gap\",\"Palisades\",\"Barnegat Bay\",\"Cape May\",\"Great Falls of the Passaic\"],\n",
