    " hist:\"Santa Fe, founded in 1610, is the oldest capital city in the United States. The first nuclear device was detonated at the Trinity Site on July 16, 1945. Admitted 1912 after 64 years as a territory.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "NY:{n:\"New York\",cap:\"Albany\",big:\"New York City\",adm:\"July 26, 1788\",ord:11,pop:20002427,pr:4,area:54555,ar:27,nick:\"Empire State\",reg:\"Northeast\",div:\"Middle Atlantic\",tz:\"Eastern\",\n",
    " hi:[\"Mount Marcy\",5344],lo:[\"Atlantic Ocean\",0],np:[],\n",
    " geo:\"The Adirondack Park covers about six million acres, the largest protected area in the contiguous United States, larger than Yellowstone, Yosemite, Grand Canyon, Glacier and Everglades combined. The Finger Lakes were gouged by glaciers; Niagara Falls carries the outflow of four Great Lakes.\",\n",
    " feat:[\"Adirondack Mountains\",\"Niagara Falls\",\"Finger Lakes\",\"Catskill Mountains\",\"Hudson Valley\",\"Long Island\"],\n",
    " riv:[\"Hudson\",\"Mohawk\",\"St. Lawrence\",\"Genesee\",\"Delaware\"],rng:[\"Adirondacks\",\"Catskills\",\"Taconic Mountains\"],\n",
    " cty:[\"New York\",\"Buffalo\",\"Yonkers\",\"Rochester\",\"Syracuse\"],\n",
    " econ:\"Global finance and media in New York City, health care and education, tourism, and dairy farming upstate.\",\n",
    " hist:\"The Erie Canal, opened 1825, tied the Great Lakes to the Atlantic and made New York the nation's leading port. Ellis Island processed roughly twelve million immigrants between 1892 and 1954.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "NC:{n:\"North Carolina\",cap:\"Raleigh\",big:\"Charlotte\",adm:\"November 21, 1789\",ord:12,pop:11197968,pr:9,area:53819,ar:28,nick:\"Tar Heel State\",reg:\"South\",div:\"South Atlantic\",tz:\"Eastern\",\n",
