    " geo:\"Mount Mitchell is the highest point in the United States east of the Mississippi. The state falls in bands from the Blue Ridge through the Piedmont to a Coastal Plain fringed by the Outer Banks, a chain of barrier islands standing as much as 30 miles offshore.\",\n",
