    " cty:[\"Oklahoma City\",\"Tulsa\",\"Norman\",\"Broken Arrow\",\"Edmond\"],\n",
    " econ:\"Oil and natural gas, aviation maintenance at Tulsa, cattle and winter wheat, and wind generation.\",\n",
    " hist:\"Designated Indian Territory, the destination of the forced removals of the 1830s. The Land Run of April 22, 1889 opened it to settlement; those who entered early were the 'Sooners.' Thirty-eight federally recognized tribes are headquartered here.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "OR:{n:\"Oregon\",cap:\"Salem\",big:\"Portland\",adm:\"February 14, 1859\",ord:33,pop:4273586,pr:27,area:98379,ar:9,nick:\"Beaver State\",reg:\"West\",div:\"Pacific\",tz:\"Pacific / Mountain (southeastern corner)\",\n",
    " hi:[\"Mount Hood\",11249],lo:[\"Pacific Ocean\",0],np:[\"Crater Lake\"],\n",
    " geo:\"The Cascades divide a wet, forested west from a high desert east that receives under ten inches of rain. Crater Lake is the deepest lake in the United States at 1,943 feet, filling the caldera left when Mount Mazama collapsed about 7,700 years ago.\",\n",
    " feat:[\"Crater Lake\",\"Columbia River Gorge\",\"Mount Hood\",\"Oregon Dunes\",\"Painted Hills\",\"Hells Canyon\"],\n",
