    " hist:\"The Black Hills were guaranteed to the Lakota by the Fort Laramie Treaty of 1868 and seized after gold was found in 1874. In 1980 the Supreme Court held the taking unlawful; the compensation has never been accepted.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "TN:{n:\"Tennessee\",cap:\"Nashville\",big:\"Nashville\",adm:\"June 1, 1796\",ord:16,pop:7315076,pr:15,area:42144,ar:36,nick:\"Volunteer State\",reg:\"South\",div:\"East South Central\",tz:\"Eastern (east) / Central (most)\",\n",
    " hi:[\"Kuwohi (formerly Clingmans Dome)\",6643],lo:[\"Mississippi River\",178],np:[\"Great Smoky Mountains (shared with North Carolina)\"],\n",
    " geo:\"Six distinct regions run west to east, from the Mississippi bottomlands across the Highland Rim and Nashville Basin to the Cumberland Plateau and the Unaka Mountains. Great Smoky Mountains is by a wide margin the most visited national park in the country.\",\n",
