    " hist:\"Last state to secede and the first readmitted. Reelfoot Lake was formed when the New Madrid earthquakes of 1811-12 caused the Mississippi to run backward. The Tennessee Valley Authority, created in 1933, electrified the region.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "TX:{n:\"Texas\",cap:\"Austin\",big:\"Houston\",adm:\"December 29, 1845\",ord:28,pop:31709821,pr:2,area:268596,ar:2,nick:\"Lone Star State\",reg:\"South\",div:\"West South Central\",tz:\"Central / Mountain (far west)\",\n",
    " hi:[\"Guadalupe Peak\",8751],lo:[\"Gulf of Mexico\",0],np:[\"Big Bend\",\"Guadalupe Mountains\"],\n",
    " geo:\"Spans four major physiographic provinces: the Gulf Coastal Plain, the Interior Lowlands, the Great Plains, and the Basin and Range. El Paso is closer to San Diego than to Beaumont. The state operates its own electrical grid, largely separate from the two national interconnections.\",\n",
