    " econ:\"The largest energy producer in the nation; petrochemicals along the Gulf, semiconductors, aerospace at Johnson Space Center, cattle and cotton, and the busiest land ports with Mexico.\",\n",
    " hist:\"An independent republic from 1836 to 1845 and the only state admitted by treaty of annexation rather than through territorial organization. The Spindletop gusher of 1901 opened the modern petroleum age.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "UT:{n:\"Utah\",cap:\"Salt Lake City\",big:\"Salt Lake City\",adm:\"January 4, 1896\",ord:45,pop:3538904,pr:30,area:84897,ar:13,nick:\"Beehive State\",reg:\"West\",div:\"Mountain\",tz:\"Mountain\",\n",
