    " econ:\"Technology along the Wasatch Front, copper at Bingham Canyon (one of the largest excavations ever made), outdoor recreation, and tourism.\",\n",
    " hist:\"Settled by Latter-day Saint pioneers from 1847. Statehood was withheld for nearly fifty years over the practice of plural marriage and granted in 1896 after it was renounced. The transcontinental railroad was joined at Promontory Summit in 1869. The Uintas are the only major range in the country running east to west.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "VT:{n:\"Vermont\",cap:\"Montpelier\",big:\"Burlington\",adm:\"March 4, 1791\",ord:14,pop:644663,pr:50,area:9616,ar:45,nick:\"Green Mountain State\",reg:\"Northeast\",div:\"New England\",tz:\"Eastern\",\n",
