    " cty:[\"Virginia Beach\",\"Chesapeake\",\"Norfolk\",\"Arlington\",\"Richmond\"],\n",
    " econ:\"Federal contracting and defense, including the Pentagon and Naval Station Norfolk, the largest naval base in the world. Northern Virginia data centers carry a substantial share of global internet traffic; shipbuilding at Newport News.\",\n",
    " hist:\"Jamestown, 1607, was the first permanent English settlement in North America. Eight presidents were born here, more than any other state. The Civil War effectively ended at Appomattox Court House in April 1865.\"},\n",
    "\n",
    "WA:{n:\"Washington\",cap:\"Olympia\",big:\"Seattle\",adm:\"November 11, 1889\",ord:42,pop:8001020,pr:13,area:71298,ar:18,nick:\"Evergreen State\",reg:\"West\",div:\"Pacific\",tz:\"Pacific\",\n",
    " hi:[\"Mount Rainier\",14411],lo:[\"Pacific Ocean\",0],np:[\"Mount Rainier\",\"North Cascades\",\"Olympic\"],\n",
    " geo:\"The Cascades split a maritime west from an arid Columbia Plateau east. The Hoh Rain Forest receives over twelve feet of rain a year while Yakima, 150 miles away, gets eight inches. Mount Rainier carries more glacial ice than any other peak in the contiguous United States.\",\n",
